From 0c6d1f16f82d553ee5c88a2ec95a8a0e38676f30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:07:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/65] Fix SAS/C build errors; port Open_ResourceFile

SAS/C 6.58 reported a redeclared struct GfxRecord, an int return in
H029+$1308 and an undefined GfxBase. GfxRecord now lives in
gfx_record.h, the return is computed in an s16, and cok.h includes the
graphics/gfxbase.h, graphics/view.h and intuition/preferences.h headers.

Also ports H028+$05FA Open_ResourceFile with its helpers ($01C6 disk
request, $0408 name split, $0576 open attempt), the H026 string
routines it uses and the H021 AutoRequest adapter. On the host, AmigaDOS
names are resolved case-insensitively below COK_DATA, and AutoRequest
waits for Retry/Cancel in the SDL window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
